"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nA spot everyone seems to visit when they come to Sydney.  \nBuilt in 1898, the Romanesque architecture and stained glass make it a building that truly captures the grandeur of Western design.\n\nThere was a free photo booth event running inside the building.  \nWe waited a bit, but it was fun and the print quality came out better than expected — very satisfying.\n\nThere are also several restaurants and cafes inside, so dining there would be a great option if you get the chance.\n\nInside the building, you'll find the Royal Clock that moves on the hour and the Great Australian Clock depicting Australian history.  \nAdmission is free, and guided tours run on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Sundays at 11:30 AM.  \nThe building narrowly escaped demolition in 1959 and was fully restored by 1986 to become what it is today.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"